+## HTTPS
+
+To serve the REST API, UI, and gRPC endpoint with TLS, configure a certificate and its private key:
+
+```yaml
+server:
+  protocol: https
+  https_port: 443
+  grpc_port: 9000
+  cert_file: /etc/flipt/tls/cert.pem
+  cert_key: /etc/flipt/tls/key.pem
+```
+
+Flipt checks that both files exist at startup and loads the certificate and key before opening a listener. With `protocol: http`, the REST API and UI continue to use `http_port` and gRPC uses plaintext.
+
 ## Databases
 
 Flipt supports both [SQLite](https://www.sqlite.org/index.html) and [Postgres](https://www.postgresql.org/) databases as of `v0.5.0`.
